Cell["\<\
All diagrams contain 4 internal fermion lines, 1 internal gluon line and two \
gluon-fermion vertices and a qed vertex. The prefactors missing from my \
amplitudes are:
Fermion line -> i delta_{ij}
Gluon line -> -i delta_{ab}
qcd vertex -> -i g_s (t^a)_{ij}
qed vertex -> -i e Q (note this Q changes from diagram to diagram depending \
on which quark the photon propagator connects to, with Qb=Qs)
The single sign factor (denoted by SF) common to all diagrams is\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.948184761602482*^9, 3.9481849872585373`*^9}, {
  3.948185044094693*^9, 3.948185105380815*^9}, {3.948185221455556*^9, 
  3.9481852217387667`*^9}, {3.9481853581362963`*^9, 3.948185378101635*^9}, {
  3.948187145075811*^9, 3.94818714632265*^9}, {3.948187192772174*^9, 
  3.9481872007425957`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b6e6a42a-f17c-448f-852c-\
fc8265f1cea2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"SF", "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", "\[ImaginaryI]", ")"}], "^", "4"}], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"-", "\[ImaginaryI]"}], ")"}], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "\[ImaginaryI]"}], " ", "gs"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "\[ImaginaryI]"}], " ", "e"}], ")"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.948185116679331*^9, 3.9481851604083843`*^9}, {
  3.948185223581573*^9, 3.948185223860746*^9}, {3.948187149336472*^9, 
  3.9481871500178633`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[13]:=",ExpressionUUID->"436007f0-cf16-47b8-b691-bd7b3e3e1d72"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"e", " ", 
  SuperscriptBox["gs", "2"]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9481851704958572`*^9, 3.948185224901828*^9, {3.948187133897541*^9, 
   3.9481871506039143`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"Out[13]=",ExpressionUUID->"49cf0101-a2b9-4ed7-8e2f-5d6de9e6f433"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
There are then two different colour structures for operator 1. The first for \
diagrams a-d and the second for diagram e. I used diagram c1 to determine CF1 \
and diagram e1 to compute CF2\
\>", "Text",
